WEBVTT


00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:09.358
Would you like to see before, you know...


00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.035
Yeah.


00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:22.913
Brian? Who's this?


00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:25.549
You know, I asked myself the same thing
when my dad passed.


00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:26.874
I said, "Who is this man?"


00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.036
No, no, Brian. Who's this in the coffin?


00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:31.993
- Because that's not my father.
- Are you sure?


00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:34.315
Are you asking me if I'm sure
I know what my father looks like?


00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.396
No, people make mistakes
in a time of grief, Aaron.


00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:38.556
Look at the damn body, man.


00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:41.269
Oh, shit.


00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:43.356
- You got Jackie Chan in there!
- Okay, listen...


00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:46.119
Come on, Brian.
You know what my father looks like.


00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:47.355
We are very scattered today.


00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:48.913
This type of thing almost never happens.


00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:50.837
- Almost never happens?
- I said that out loud?


00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:53.599
It's not Burger King.
You can't just mess up my order.


00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:55.517
Please, just calm down.
I think I know where he is.


00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:56.914
You think?


00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:00.589
If my dad's not in this coffin in one hour,
then you have to take his place.


00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:03.029
- You got it?
- Don't worry. I'll get him back.


00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:07.472
I promise that. He's in one of two places.
I think it's the second place.


00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:10.672
Listen, okay, guys? Let's pack this up.
Close this.


00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:12.153
Let's go, let's get out of here.


00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:16.114
Wait a minute, before we move...
Okay. Did I give you my keys?


00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:19.359
No. They in the car.
I left the damn keys in the car.


00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:21.391
Let's go, guys. I think it's on.


00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:24.114
If you're so antsy about being here,
why'd you come out in the first place?


00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:26.549
- You know why.
- I hate funerals.


00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.879
All about death, death, death.


00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:32.470
I don't think funerals are designed
for anybody to like, Norman.


00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:34.033
I suppose.


00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:36.720
I don't want a regular funeral
when it's my time to go, you know.


00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:38.637
I want my life celebrated.


00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:42.150
Like Anna Nicole Smith, Richard Nixon,
somebody big and powerful.


00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:43.998
I want mine to be the saddest day ever.


00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:47.032
Stock market should crash,
factories shut down,


00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:48.752
girls crying in the streets.


00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:52.236
That kind of thing. An eclipse would be nice.


00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:54.316
- Come on.
- What?


00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:56.635
You still smoking after all of
those warnings and stuff out there?


00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:59.399
No, Norman, stop, all right.
You used to smoke.


00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:00.555
We used to smoke together.


00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:03.114
I used to piss my pants and then I stopped.


00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:05.879
I got my own problems to worry about
without worrying about your damn smoking.


00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:07.956
Come on, Norman.
What problems you got, man?


00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:11.277
- I told you! My rash!
- Got to use condoms, papa.


00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:14.278
- On my hand, dude.
- You still have to use a condom, Norman.


00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:15.515
That's the first line of defence.


00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:18.234
This shit ain't normal. Look at it.


00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:21.393
- Fuck. That ain't a rash, man.
- What you think it is?


00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:24.876
I don't know, but it's very splotchy.


00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:28.436
Splotchy? I hate splotchy.
I'm gonna pass away, I'm gonna die!


00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:29.959
- Nah.
- And I'm so damn young!


00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:32.436
They brought the wrong body.


00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:35.279
Honey, did you hear me?
They brought the wrong body.


00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:36.958
Oh, my God!
Well, do they know where he is?


00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:38.513
They think so.


00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:42.476
I told you.
I told you not to use the Marshalls,


00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:44.511
but, no, you wanted to keep it all
in the neighbourhood.


00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:47.518
Don't rub it in, not today.
I got too much to worry about.


00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:51.189
Dad insisted on having his funeral
at home, so now I just can't escape it.


00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:52.878
Death is everywhere.


00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:54.956
Baby, no. No, it's not.


00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:56.513
Mom won't stop crying.


00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:58.551
- Ryan hasn't helped out.
- Not like he ever does.


00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:00.875
Plus on top of that, I got to worry
about this whole eulogy thing.


00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:04.356
I am sure it'll be the best eulogy
anybody's ever heard.


00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:05.708
Doesn't matter.


00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:09.071
All anybody's gonna be thinking is,
"Why isn't Ryan doing the eulogy?


00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:11.156
"Step aside and let the writer
say a few words."


00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:12.315
Even I'm gonna be thinking it.


00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:15.113
Why don't you just let him do it then?


00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:17.514
So, now you want Ryan to do the eulogy?


00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:18.675
No. I'm just saying...


00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:20.756
You're just saying that you wanna
hear Ryan's eulogy.


00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.108
No. You're the oldest, so...


00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:24.196
So, the only reason I should do it
is because I'm old.


00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:26.038
Aaron, calm down.


00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:29.831
I think that you are every bit
as good a writer as your brother.


00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:33.919
I just think that you need to let
someone actually read your book.


00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:35.519
It's not ready yet.


00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:38.108
Okay, fine. But don't forget,
we close on the house next week.


00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:41.679
- I know.
- I mean, I love your mom,


00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:43.711
but I am so ready to move.


00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:46.308
I know, honey,
but we just got to get through today, okay?


00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:47.668
Exactly.


00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:50.157
I know this is rough.


00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:52.596
But it's the last day of my cycle.


00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:55.837
And I'm 37 years old, so we need to try to,


00:06:55.960 --> 00:07:00.476
you know, we need to do it,
at least once today, okay?


00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:01.669
- Babe.
- Yeah?


00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:06.191
You're gonna have to switch that cycle
down to low for now, just for now.


00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:09.071
Can we at least find the body first?


00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:16.558
- Are you okay?
- Yeah, absolutely.


00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:20.908
Okay, I'm a... I'm a little nervous.


00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:23.033
Why, because you're gonna see
my dad again?


00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:26.391
I just don't think I've ever been
so openly hated by anyone before.


00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:27.669
Even my seventh graders aren't that mean.


00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:30.712
I think he's gonna be more concerned today
that his brother just died than be...


00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:33.070
- Babe.
- I'm sorry, baby. It's the traffic.


00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:35.430
Right. Anyway, when I tell him
that we're getting married,


00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:37.869
he's just gonna have to accept you. I...


00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:39.991
- Jesus! Are you okay?
- Oh, my God.


00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:41.473
- You asshole!
- Fuck you, bitch.


00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:44.273
Oh, yeah, flip me off.
Can't you see there's a traffic jam?


00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:45.958
You poke your eye out,
your father's gonna kill me.


00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:47.798
- Oscar, baby.
- Yes.


00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:48.989
- Look at me.
- Okay.


00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:50.553
- Relax. Okay?
- All right.


00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:52.875
Everything is fine. Okay? Breathe.


00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:54.149
Okay.


00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:57.269
- Better?
- Better.


00:07:57.400 --> 00:07:59.118
Oh, good. It's okay.


00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:01.269
Fuck you!


00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:07.640
I think you'll find that
everything is in perfect order.


00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:10.558
Oh, so, now you wanna be professional.


00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:12.272
You got your keys?
You got your BlackBerry?


00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:14.356
Because once we bury him,
we not gonna dig him back up


00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:15.833
just so you can tweet.


00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:17.552
Look, I'm trying, okay?


00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:19.352
Hey, how is your mother holding up, Aaron?


00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:21.038
She's fine. She's in great health.


00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:22.593
- There's no more business here.
- Good.


00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:24.358
What about your Uncle Russell?
He wasn't doing that well.


00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:25.469
- How's he doing?
- Bye.


00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:28.114
Okay, I'm just asking.
It's conversation, that's all.


00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:31.152
I'm here if you need me, you know that.
Thank you for everything.


00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:32.508
- Michelle, come here.
- Bye, Brian.


00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:33.914
You don't have to come.


00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:37.795
I'm just saying, everybody knows
that the Colonel stole that recipe


00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:40.798
for fried chicken from a slave named Jubalai.


00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:44.515
Now, I give him credit for the coleslaw,
but that's it.


00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:48.350
Hey, buddy! How you doing?


00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:51.517
I need a favour.
I need you to pick up Uncle Russell.


00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:54.074
Yeah, I know it's a hassle,
but you're the closest.


00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:58.478
- Damn! He's always in a bad mood.
- Just say you'll do it. We'll do it.


00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:02.878
It's not a mood if he's always in it.
It's his personality. Can you do it?


00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:04.877
All right, I'll do it.


00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:10.955
Hey, Mama. How you holding up?


00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:14.477
There were so many things
we wanted to do still.


00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:17.309
Travel.
We were going to Australia and China.


00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:18.429
He wanted to go to Thailand.


00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:20.471
Oh, come on, Ma,
you're not gonna fly 25 hours.


00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:23.637
That's not the point.
I haven't been feeling well.


00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:26.479
Who knows how long
I'm gonna live without him?


00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:29.273
It might make a difference
if I had a grandchild


00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:32.472
who could take my mind off
of everything, but...


00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:34.957
- Oh, well.
- Cynthia, we are trying.


00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:39.153
I know what you're trying to do, Michelle,
all hours of the day and night, trying.


00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:41.510
But it doesn't seem to be working,
now does it?


00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:44.359
- Where's Ryan? Have you talked to him yet?
- He should be here soon.


00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:48.268
Just to see his face
would make me feel so much better.


00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:51.631
Oh, I have missed him so much. My baby.


00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:53.838
Do you need me to do something, Cynthia?


00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:57.077
You could take your hand off
my husband's coffin.


00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:59.509
You are leaving a smudge mark.


00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:04.995
Is she shooting us the finger?
Or is she just waving?


00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:07.475
That's nice, ladies! Thank you!


00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:11.869
- There he is.
- What?


00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:13.194
- He's okay.
- He's gonna need assistance?


00:10:13.320 --> 00:10:14.833
He's just grumpy.


00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:17.474
You got to know how to handle him.


00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:21.678
Oh, he looks kind of sweet.


00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:22.949
- Hi, Uncle Russell!
- Hi, Uncle Russell!


00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:24.479
You remember me? I'm Norman.


00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:26.795
I came to pick you up
and take you to the funeral.


00:10:26.920 --> 00:10:30.879
Where the fuck you been, you fat bastard?
You took any longer, I'd be dead, too!


00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:33.195
Shit, good thing you know
how to handle him.


00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:35.197
Would you like to ride shotgun?


00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:37.155
<i>Stop the game, all right?</i>


00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:39.669
...take this missile in your ass.


00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:41.313
<i>- Listen.</i>
- Yes, the pills. I have them.


00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:43.317
- They're right here.
<i>- All right, cool. Can I come and get them?</i>


00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:46.352
- I have a funeral to go to. Shit!
<i>- Whatever. Man, I'll come over there.</i>


00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:47.879
- Fuck.
<i>- Did you try them?</i>


00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:49.592
No, no, I'm not gonna try them. I made them.


00:10:49.720 --> 00:10:51.119
<i>But they're good, right? The stuff's good?</i>


00:10:51.240 --> 00:10:53.549
I got to go.
Never get high on your own supply.


00:10:53.680 --> 00:10:56.194
And, dude, this shit's gonna
blow your mind, I guarantee it.


00:10:56.320 --> 00:10:59.118
You'll love it. All right, got to go. Bye.


00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:03.192
Do you always open the door half naked?


00:11:03.320 --> 00:11:05.390
Come on, Jeff, we're gonna be late.


00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:06.919
All I got to do is just put some pants on.


00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:10.237
And this is my house, so...
You all right, man?


00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:13.715
- He's fine. He's just freaking out.
- Is he okay?


00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:17.230
- A car almost ran into us, and I was yelling.
- And this guy just jumped right in our lane.


00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:18.713
- I didn't see him.
- He did, he totally did.


00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:20.592
- I'm sorry, baby, I...
- No, baby, it's fine. It's fine, okay?


00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:22.676
You guys are funny.
Hey, what do you think?


00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:23.755
- Yes, no?
- No.


00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:26.633
- Go put on your pants, please.
- All right.


00:11:26.760 --> 00:11:28.637
And make sure they're black, Jeffrey!


00:11:28.760 --> 00:11:30.113
Okay, Mom.


00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:33.031
- I'm so hungry.
- God, my heart is racing.


00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:35.549
I don't know what's wrong with me.


00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:41.919
Oh, here. Take this one.
It'll calm you down. Jeff won't mind.


00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:43.469
What do you mean, take one of those?
What is that?


00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:47.479
It's Valium. I used to take it all the time.
It's gonna make you feel better, I promise.


00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:49.113
- Valium, are you sure?
- Yeah.


00:11:49.240 --> 00:11:50.229
- Yes.
- You know, I shouldn't be taking


00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:51.315
someone else's pills, right?


00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:53.317
- No, it's okay.
- I got to drive and...


00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:58.514
Babe, I'll drive. All right?
Just open wide. There we go. Take...


00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:01.876
Let's do this.


00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:05.672
- Oh, my keys.
- Jeff, you're wearing sneakers?


00:12:05.800 --> 00:12:07.438
- They're black, Elaine.
- But they're sneakers, Jeff.


00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:09.073
Is he gonna be any less dead
if I'm not wearing sneakers?


00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:12.237
- Forget it. Let's just go. Can I just...
- No, I got it.


00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:13.475
Okay.


00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:18.275
- Come on, Jeff.
- I'm coming. I'm coming.


00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:20.231
- We're waiting.
- Oh, shoot!


00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:24.795
I still can't believe he's gone.


00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:28.991
You can't understand death
until you've given life.


00:12:29.920 --> 00:12:34.118
- Hey, Mama.
- Ryan, my baby!


00:12:34.240 --> 00:12:35.389
Hey.


00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:39.432
Mama, I know this is hard,
but it's gonna be okay,


00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:40.754
and we're gonna get through it.


00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:44.714
Oh, Ryan, you always know
exactly what to say, always!


00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:46.990
I guess if people died every week,
we'd see you all the time.


00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:49.475
- Hey, big bro. How you doing?
- Holding up.


00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:51.591
- How was your flight, Ryan?
- It was okay.


00:12:51.720 --> 00:12:55.918
But I had to buy the seat next to me.
I just can't do the small talk any more.


00:12:56.040 --> 00:13:00.591
And while I'm sitting there, up in first class,
they march all the broke people through.


00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:05.236
And a couple of them eyeballing me,
mad because I'm snacking on warm nuts.


00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:10.038
So I'm like, "Take your broke,
no-nuts ass to the back of the plane."


00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:12.674
Plus, there was tons of turbulence,


00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:15.109
but I guess that's the thing
about flying first class.


00:13:15.240 --> 00:13:21.270
No matter how much you pay,
if the plane crashes, you still end up dead.


00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:28.589
- End up dead!
- I'll make sure she's okay.


00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:30.950
- Please.
- End up dead!


00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:33.672
You always know just what to say.


00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:35.119
My bad.


00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:39.236
Hey. I love it when you come
to family functions, man.


00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:41.271
Because Dad takes his pure hate out on you.


00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:43.755
- Jeff.
- I'm joking. Oscar.


00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:46.393
You okay?


00:13:47.320 --> 00:13:48.514
Was there a dog in here just now?


00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:50.119
- What?
- What?


00:13:50.920 --> 00:13:54.071
Like a Dalmatian or a Schnauzer?


00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:57.670
- Honey, what are you talking about?
- I don't know.


00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:03.592
It's just a shame that somebody
has to die to get the family together.


00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:08.073
It was hard to see Dad like this.
He's in a better place now, right?


00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:10.998
- He was sick a long time.
- Since when does dead beat sick?


00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:14.954
You know what I mean.
This is why I try not to get close to people.


00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:18.072
- Too much emotion involved.
- Guess that's why you never call.


00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:21.272
Some families see each other all the time,
some meet up at funerals.


00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:22.389
That's just us.


00:14:22.520 --> 00:14:27.833
Hey, listen, I know this is a bad time,
but I'm gonna need that money.


00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:29.879
- Shit.
- We're splitting these costs, right?


00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.150
