No! I'm not gonna stay out of it.
This is my life.


01:16:14.120 --> 01:16:17.396
You don't like it, too bad.
But I'm gonna tell you something.


01:16:17.520 --> 01:16:19.351
If you wanna have me
and my child in your life,


01:16:19.480 --> 01:16:22.438
you better change your attitude.
You got that?


01:16:24.840 --> 01:16:27.673
- I love you.
- My little girl.


01:16:28.920 --> 01:16:29.989
Yeah.


01:16:31.720 --> 01:16:33.472
I love you, too, Dad.


01:16:36.600 --> 01:16:38.511
What the fuck's going on in here?


01:16:38.640 --> 01:16:40.676
- Sorry, Uncle Russell.
- Yeah, sorry about that.


01:16:40.800 --> 01:16:43.917
Somebody was on the roof,
and we just had to get him off.


01:16:44.040 --> 01:16:45.951
Okay, I got your pants.
I got your pants. Hold on.


01:16:46.080 --> 01:16:49.197
Never mind that. What about
that dead body you dragged in here?


01:16:49.320 --> 01:16:50.389
- What...
- Dead body?


01:16:50.520 --> 01:16:52.158
- No dead body.
- Hey, don't mess with me!


01:16:52.280 --> 01:16:55.272
I know a dead man when I see one.
I live in a goddamn retirement home.


01:16:55.400 --> 01:16:57.550
Let's go, God damn it.
It smells in this room. Shit!


01:16:58.400 --> 01:17:01.039
- How's the... How's the skin thing?
- I don't know.


01:17:01.160 --> 01:17:04.118
I'm more concerned with the shit smell.
Can you tell?


01:17:04.240 --> 01:17:07.949
Yeah, yeah, but the thing on your hand,
you just put a little vinegar on it.


01:17:08.080 --> 01:17:09.911
That'll clear it right up.
It's an old family secret.


01:17:10.040 --> 01:17:12.600
The shit thing, I can't help you with.


01:17:12.760 --> 01:17:14.830
I would recommend a shower or a bath.


01:17:14.960 --> 01:17:16.871
- Thanks.
- You're welcome.


01:17:17.520 --> 01:17:20.637
- I'm sorry about the whole Elaine thing, man.
- It's okay.


01:17:20.760 --> 01:17:24.036
Did you hear she's gonna have a kid?
Can you see me as a dad?


01:17:24.160 --> 01:17:25.354
- No.
- No.


01:17:27.280 --> 01:17:28.793
Well, this shit's been crazy.


01:17:28.920 --> 01:17:33.630
You have people falling out of the casket,
you got people hanging off the roof.


01:17:34.280 --> 01:17:35.474
Can I have the keys?
I'm gonna go wait in the car.


01:17:35.600 --> 01:17:37.158
- What?
- I'm just tired.


01:17:37.280 --> 01:17:39.430
- Okay.
- Okay.


01:17:39.560 --> 01:17:40.595
Hey.


01:17:42.200 --> 01:17:44.316
- Love you.
- Hey, I love you, too.


01:17:44.440 --> 01:17:46.317
I saw him! He was dead!


01:17:46.920 --> 01:17:49.070
- I know you did, Uncle Russell. We all did.
- Shit.


01:17:49.200 --> 01:17:53.159
No, dumbshit. In the bathroom.
He was in the bathroom dead.


01:17:53.280 --> 01:17:56.352
I cannot believe
what a nightmare today has been.


01:17:56.480 --> 01:18:00.109
I don't know, I think it's kind of exciting.
For a funeral.


01:18:01.800 --> 01:18:06.794
- Listen, about that stuff earlier, I...
- I know, we'll work it out.


01:18:07.120 --> 01:18:08.633
- Agreed?
- Agreed.


01:18:08.760 --> 01:18:09.715
Let's just get through this day


01:18:09.840 --> 01:18:12.513
and then we'll worry
about the rest of our lives.


01:18:12.640 --> 01:18:14.596
I still have to give this eulogy.


01:18:14.720 --> 01:18:16.870
After everything I found out.


01:18:17.000 --> 01:18:19.200
We've really got
to get this damn thing started.


01:18:19.200 --> 01:18:20.076
We've really got
to get this damn thing started.


01:18:20.760 --> 01:18:23.832
Look, we're gonna have
to zip through this thing now, son.


01:18:23.960 --> 01:18:25.712
I mean, I've already missed a funeral
and two christenings.


01:18:25.840 --> 01:18:29.355
- Yeah, yeah, sure. Let's... Let's start.
- Okay. You want a open casket?


01:18:29.480 --> 01:18:30.674
- No!
- No.


01:18:31.360 --> 01:18:32.634
All right.


01:18:34.720 --> 01:18:36.836
Everybody in their seats now.


01:18:37.280 --> 01:18:38.429
- You with the hat?
- Yeah?


01:18:38.560 --> 01:18:39.754
Sit on down.


01:18:39.880 --> 01:18:42.553
Now, I'd like to apologise
on behalf of the family


01:18:42.680 --> 01:18:45.274
for all of the distractions.


01:18:46.280 --> 01:18:50.512
Aaron, the oldest son, would like to say
a few words about his father.


01:18:51.520 --> 01:18:52.794
Thank you.


01:19:00.880 --> 01:19:01.949
Okay.


01:19:03.880 --> 01:19:08.078
"My father was an exceptional man.


01:19:15.400 --> 01:19:18.278
"He was born in 19..."


01:19:20.040 --> 01:19:22.554
- What the hell is going on now?
- There's someone in there.


01:19:22.680 --> 01:19:24.830
I knew it! I knew it!


01:19:24.960 --> 01:19:29.238
"He was born in 1930..."


01:19:30.920 --> 01:19:31.989
Shit.


01:19:33.160 --> 01:19:34.229
Shit.


01:19:36.200 --> 01:19:37.758
What the fuck!


01:19:37.880 --> 01:19:40.553
What the fuck you doing
in my father's coffin?


01:19:45.800 --> 01:19:48.109
Edward, I miss you!


01:19:48.720 --> 01:19:50.995
Leave me with my Edward!


01:19:51.120 --> 01:19:54.192
My picture. My beautiful memories!


01:19:57.520 --> 01:19:59.636
No, Mama, don't. Give me...


01:20:00.720 --> 01:20:02.312
You bastard!


01:20:11.400 --> 01:20:13.436
My father!


01:20:14.760 --> 01:20:20.278
My father was an exceptional man.


01:20:23.600 --> 01:20:25.477
Did he have his faults?


01:20:28.080 --> 01:20:29.149
Yeah.


01:20:31.160 --> 01:20:34.197
But he worked hard for his family.


01:20:34.320 --> 01:20:36.709
All I wanted to do today


01:20:36.840 --> 01:20:42.836
was tell him how much we all loved,
cherished and respected him.


01:20:43.800 --> 01:20:46.234
Is that really too much to ask for?


01:20:47.040 --> 01:20:50.874
So, maybe he loved <i>Dreamgirls</i>
more than most men.


01:20:52.400 --> 01:20:55.551
But, hey, life is complicated.


01:20:56.200 --> 01:20:57.679
We do our best.


01:20:58.720 --> 01:21:01.029
And Dad, he did his best.


01:21:02.960 --> 01:21:04.518
One thing he did


01:21:05.040 --> 01:21:07.679
was teach us to chase after our dreams.


01:21:09.400 --> 01:21:11.595
So, when you leave here today,


01:21:11.720 --> 01:21:15.793
I want you to remember my father
for who he truly was,


01:21:15.920 --> 01:21:21.199
a loving, kind, gentle man,
that never judged anyone,


01:21:22.000 --> 01:21:25.788
who never cast disparaging remarks


01:21:27.440 --> 01:21:33.470
or held prejudice against any race,
creed, gender,


01:21:34.720 --> 01:21:35.994
or height.


01:21:36.840 --> 01:21:41.231
And if I turn out to be just half the man
that my father was,


01:21:41.360 --> 01:21:45.399
then the child I'm planning on having
with my beautiful wife


01:21:47.080 --> 01:21:48.877
will be truly blessed.


01:21:55.120 --> 01:21:56.394
Thank you.


01:21:59.280 --> 01:22:00.759
Well done, son.


01:22:03.320 --> 01:22:05.231
It's gonna be good, boy.


01:22:06.880 --> 01:22:08.108
Good job.


01:22:10.560 --> 01:22:12.790
Oscar, let's not do this again.


01:22:15.560 --> 01:22:18.791
I always thought he had a little sugar
in his tank.


01:22:30.880 --> 01:22:32.711
Hey, how's Mom holding up?


01:22:32.840 --> 01:22:35.400
She's good. Resting.


01:22:36.840 --> 01:22:40.628
You know, it's gonna take a while
for her to accept dad was...


01:22:42.040 --> 01:22:43.553
You know.


01:22:43.680 --> 01:22:45.193
She'll be okay.


01:22:45.880 --> 01:22:49.395
You know, that was a pretty good send-off
you gave the old man. You wrote that?


01:22:49.520 --> 01:22:52.637
Some guy I met told me
I need to be spontaneous.


01:22:52.760 --> 01:22:55.911
Yeah, well, Dad would've been proud.
I know I was.


01:22:56.640 --> 01:22:59.552
Maybe when you're ready, you'll let me
take a look at that novel of yours.


01:22:59.680 --> 01:23:00.908
Yeah.


01:23:01.040 --> 01:23:04.077
- Yeah, I'm gonna send it to you next week.
- All right.


01:23:04.200 --> 01:23:07.272
- But you know Michelle gotta read it first.
- Okay.


01:23:07.400 --> 01:23:09.868
I'm not going through that again.


01:23:10.000 --> 01:23:12.355
All right. Well, thanks, big bro.


01:23:13.040 --> 01:23:15.634
Sure you don't wanna stay another day?


01:23:16.760 --> 01:23:19.035
Got a good Laker game coming up.


01:23:19.800 --> 01:23:21.518
- Your boy, Kobe.
- No.


01:23:22.160 --> 01:23:24.549
I'd just be feeling sad or be in the way.


01:23:24.680 --> 01:23:27.513
You know how it is.
Probably gonna get on back.


01:23:27.640 --> 01:23:30.438
You know, do my thing. Still gotta grieve.


01:23:31.440 --> 01:23:32.634
Me, too.


01:23:39.280 --> 01:23:41.874
What? A brother's gotta get to the airport.


01:23:42.000 --> 01:23:45.549
Come on, you better make sure
you don't go to jail first.


01:23:46.360 --> 01:23:47.873
- Hey.
- Ryan.


01:23:48.000 --> 01:23:49.911
- Sis.
- Baby, listen,


01:23:50.040 --> 01:23:54.079
- don't stay away so long next time, okay?
- I sure won't. All right, bro.


01:23:54.200 --> 01:23:55.838
Hey, next funeral.


01:23:57.320 --> 01:23:59.754
- Love you, man.
- Love you, too, man.


01:24:05.800 --> 01:24:07.791
Wow, I see he got his ride.


01:24:07.920 --> 01:24:10.673
Yeah. R. Kelly used the same car service.


01:24:16.160 --> 01:24:18.151
Just like candy.


01:24:23.720 --> 01:24:27.599
I am worn out. This has been a long day.


01:24:27.720 --> 01:24:29.312
A long, long day.


01:24:30.160 --> 01:24:31.957
- And guess what?
- What?


01:24:35.600 --> 01:24:37.272
Now I'm interested.


01:24:38.440 --> 01:24:42.479
No Mama. No guests. No Uncle Russell.


01:24:44.920 --> 01:24:46.990
- Where's Uncle Russell?
- He's upstairs.


01:24:47.120 --> 01:24:50.078
I gave him a couple Valium
and put him to bed.


01:24:52.160 --> 01:24:53.195
What?


01:24:54.200 --> 01:24:56.634
Shit. Man.


01:24:57.720 --> 01:24:59.915
Everything's so fucking green.

